{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966792,"nonce":"x3BfFEwIYlMhFJC19HfmGTkkQRU=","title":"FSM event codes collide with widget pointer events","message":"When a widget Stateful is bound to a `SharedState\u003cFsmStateId\u003e` (via `with_shared_state`), the Stateful still auto-registers `POINTER_DOWN`/`POINTER_UP`/`POINTER_ENTER`/`POINTER_LEAVE`/`DRAG`/`DRAG_END` handlers on the container. Each handler calls `inner.state.on_event(numeric_event_type)`. For `FsmStateId`, `on_event` looks the numeric code up against the FSM's stored transitions table.\n\n`event_types::POINTER_DOWN = 1`, `POINTER_UP = 2`, … (1..=7). DSL-defined FSM event codes used to start at 0 and increase. So any click would silently dispatch the FSM event whose code matched the pointer event — e.g. `Reset = event_code 1` collides with `POINTER_DOWN = 1`, and every click on the bound subtree quietly fired `Reset`.\n\n**Why:** the substrate originally treated `u32` event codes as a single namespace shared by widget pointer events and FSM events. Builtin widget states (`ButtonState`, `ScrollState`) deliberately encode their transitions against the pointer-event codes — that's how `:hover` works. DSL FSMs don't share that intent; their event names are arbitrary and shouldn't be reached by pointer dispatch.\n\n**How to apply:** every FSM event code in [`blinc_runtime::fsm::registry`](crates/blinc_runtime/src/fsm/registry.rs) is now offset by `FSM_EVENT_CODE_OFFSET = 0x4000_0000`. `FsmDefinition::event_code(name)` adds the offset on lookup; `publish_fsms_to_runtime_registry` in [`blinc_dsl_core`](crates/blinc_dsl_core/src/lib.rs) stores transitions with the offset. Pointer events stay in 1..=7, FSM events live above `1\u003c\u003c30` — `step_event` lookup can't cross-match. If a new DSL surface ever feeds a non-pointer numeric event into `on_event` (e.g. custom keyboard events), keep it below the offset or it'll trip the same trap.\n\nSymptom-side checklist when an FSM-driven DSL view \"loses state between interactions\":\n- look for `event=\u003csmall int\u003e` `state.on_event` writes between user interactions\n- if a transition is firing with the same numeric code as a pointer event, this gotcha is the cause","files":null}]}